package templates

// About is written in the third person on purpose.
//
// It used to be the original author's personal page: "I built itchgrep.com",
// followed by their email, Twitter, Mastodon, Discord and itch.io profile. On a
// fork run by somebody else that page is wrong twice over - it speaks as
// someone who does not operate this site, and it points support at a person who
// cannot answer for it. The credit below is the part worth keeping; the contact
// details were theirs, not this deployment's.
templ About() {
	<div id="page-content" class="prose">
		<h2>About</h2>
		<p>
			itchgrep searches <a href="https://itch.io/game-assets" target="_blank" rel="noopener">itch.io/game-assets</a>
			by text rather than by tag alone. itch.io itself only lets you browse
			the asset catalogue by picking tags, which works badly when you know
			what you want but not what somebody chose to label it.
		</p>
		<p>
			A crawler walks the public browse pages a couple of requests per
			second, builds a full-text index over roughly 100,000 assets, and
			this site queries it. Nothing is mirrored: every result links
			straight back to the asset's own itch.io page, and every purchase,
			download and page view still happens there.
		</p>
		<h2>Credit</h2>
		<p>
			itchgrep was created by
			<a href={ templ.SafeURL(AuthorURL) } target="_blank" rel="noopener">{ AuthorName }</a>,
			whose original version is at
			<a href={ templ.SafeURL(UpstreamURL) } target="_blank" rel="noopener">{ UpstreamURL }</a>.
			This site runs a fork of that work and is not operated by the
			original author, so nothing here should be taken as their doing.
		</p>
		<p>
			Their own games and assets are at
			<a href="https://winterveil.itch.io/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">winterveil.itch.io</a>.
		</p>
		<h2>Source</h2>
		<p>
			itchgrep is free software under the
			<a href="https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GNU GPL v3</a>.
			The code this site runs is at
			<a href={ templ.SafeURL(SourceURL) } target="_blank" rel="noopener">{ SourceURL }</a>.
		</p>
		<hr/>
		<p><a href="/">← Back to search</a></p>
	</div>
}
